#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096350 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4435e346-d6ad-58cd-97cb-bbd45e121759" :knowledge-point/title "Using Integration by Parts to Compute an Integral Containing a Single Logarithmic Factor"}] :question/id #uuid "12811582-7156-5b84-9ba9-5545f87894f3" :question/math-academy-id "e-3993" :question/problem "Calculate $\\displaystyle \\int \\ln{x}\\,\\textrm{d}x$." :question/worked-solution "At first, it may not look like we have two factors. Actually, we do, but one of them is implicit. The trick is to write the integral as\n\n$$\n\\int \\ln{x}\\,\\textrm{d}x = \\int \\ln{x} \\cdot 1 \\cdot \\textrm{d}x\n$$\n\nUsing this trick, we can now use integration by parts. We let\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}u = \\ln x & ⟹u^{′} = \\frac{1}{x} \\\\ v^{′} = 1 & ⟹v = x\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nNow, using the by-parts formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\int\\ln xdx &= x\\ln x - \\intx \\cdot \\frac{1}{x}dx \\\\\n&= x\\ln x - \\int1dx \\\\\n&= x\\ln x - x + C \\\\\n&= x(\\ln x - 1) + C\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096398 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "31a28451-005e-50dc-a7cf-5b666b1d7735" :knowledge-point/title "Using Integration by Parts to Compute an Integral Containing a Natural Logarithm"}] :question/id #uuid "c7373a16-c90a-5875-8b17-8724542b35ed" :question/math-academy-id "e-493" :question/problem "Evaluate $\\displaystyle \\int_{1}^{e} 4x\\ln\\left(x^3\\right) \\textrm{d}x$." :question/worked-solution "We will solve this problem using integration by parts. We start by defining $u$ and $v'$, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}u = \\ln (x^{3}) & ⟹u^{′} = \\frac{1}{x^{3}} \\cdot 3x^{2} = \\frac{3}{x} \\\\ v^{′} = 4x & ⟹v = \\int4xdx = 2x^{2}\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula of integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\int_{1}^{e}4x\\ln (x^{3})dx &= \\int_{1}^{e}uv^{′}dx \\\\\n&= \\left.uv\\right|_{1}^{e} - \\int_{1}^{e}vu^{′}dx \\\\\n&= \\ln (x^{3}) \\cdot \\left.(2x^{2})\\right|_{1}^{e} - \\int_{1}^{e}(2x^{2}) \\cdot \\frac{3}{x}dx \\\\\n&= [2(e)^{2}\\ln (e^{3}) - 2(1)^{2}\\ln (1^{3})] - 6\\int_{1}^{e}xdx \\\\\n&= 6e^{2} - \\left.6(\\frac{1}{2}x^{2})\\right|_{1}^{e} \\\\\n&= 6e^{2} - \\left.3x^{2}\\right|_{1}^{e} \\\\\n&= 6e^{2} - 3(e^{2} - 1^{2}) \\\\\n&= 3e^{2} + 3\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096399 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6c987d6e-0dd9-50fa-85a0-905c93e07413" :knowledge-point/title "Using Integration by Parts to Compute an Integral Containing an Arbitrary Logarithm"}] :question/id #uuid "672d52f6-89d8-550d-863b-7c5157d59ca3" :question/math-academy-id "e-494" :question/problem "Calculate $\\displaystyle \\int \\dfrac{\\log_4{x}}{x^3} \\,\\textrm{d}x$." :question/worked-solution "We define\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}u = \\log_{4} x & ⟹u^{′} = \\frac{1}{x\\ln 4} \\\\ v^{′} = \\frac{1}{x^{3}} & ⟹v = \\int\\frac{1}{x^{3}}dx =-\\frac{1}{2x^{2}}\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula of integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\int\\frac{\\log_{4} x}{x^{3}}dx &= \\intuv^{′}dx \\\\\n&= uv - \\intvu^{′}dx \\\\\n&= \\log_{4} x(-\\frac{1}{2x^{2}}) - \\int(-\\frac{1}{2x^{2}})\\frac{1}{x\\ln 4}dx \\\\\n&=-\\frac{1}{2x^{2}}\\log_{4} x + \\frac{1}{2\\ln 4}\\int\\frac{1}{x^{3}}dx \\\\\n&=-\\frac{\\ln x}{2x^{2}\\ln 4} + \\frac{1}{2\\ln 4}(-\\frac{1}{2x^{2}}) + C \\\\\n&=-\\frac{\\ln x}{2x^{2}\\ln 4} - \\frac{1}{4x^{2}\\ln 4} + C \\\\\n&=-\\frac{2\\ln x + 1}{4x^{2}\\ln 4} + C\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that in the above calculation we used the change of base formula\n\n$$\n\\log_4{x}=\\dfrac{\\ln{x}}{\\ln{4}}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096977 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6c987d6e-0dd9-50fa-85a0-905c93e07413" :knowledge-point/title "Using Integration by Parts to Compute an Integral Containing an Arbitrary Logarithm"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "98b283cb-6c59-5a0f-8573-54fa471f7356" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{\\ln x + 2}{x^{2}\\ln 3} + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186094269} {:answer/id #uuid "bb8dfc3b-eb1f-52e4-ace6-343a7c46618a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2\\ln x + 1}{x^{2}\\ln 3} + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186094270} {:answer/id #uuid "e81bf1f8-844b-5dd4-a69e-d1ce8972fa3a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\ln x + 2}{4x^{2}\\ln 3} + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186094271} {:answer/id #uuid "fd86a01e-9451-55d1-a019-988a3ace1a4b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\ln x + 1}{2x^{2}\\ln 3} + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186094272} {:answer/id #uuid "67de0f22-0b54-5707-bb69-7cd76166d425" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{2\\ln x + 1}{4x^{2}\\ln 3} + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186094273}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "67de0f22-0b54-5707-bb69-7cd76166d425" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{2\\ln x + 1}{4x^{2}\\ln 3} + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186094273} :answer-field/id #uuid "41f9df16-6da1-5faf-9b43-d505c6ce5157" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186094268}] :question/id #uuid "ce071f41-118b-504d-a520-d6c46fbbaaf1" :question/math-academy-id "q-12570" :question/problem "Calculate $\\displaystyle \\int\\frac{\\log_{3} x}{x^{3}}dx$."}]}
